Cell[TextData[{
 "The two runs are then simply cheap-then-expensive on those independent \
values. On the sequential one we hook a \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]cheap\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] apply. Presently we chose this to be(Together[# /. \
Gen@sol[$rule, func] /. Gen@sol[$rule, const]] &): \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]expand everything and apply ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Together"]], "paclet:ref/Together"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->{"InlineFormula"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "654463b0-590c-45e5-92c5-e464c24fdfc3"],
 "\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. After that we run the more \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]expensive\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Simplify"]], "paclet:ref/Simplify"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->{"InlineFormula"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "3cae9e3c-1d5e-4a8c-bcb3-b08dcf4c1ca3"],
 " on top of that intermediate result. If one prefers to keep that step as \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]cheap\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] as possible simply \
provide ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Identity"]], "paclet:ref/Identity"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->{"InlineFormula"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "56a6a41c-c975-48d3-af09-9a6d39e7fd1b"],
 " as the sequential ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Map"]], "paclet:ref/Map"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->{"InlineFormula"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "0de1487d-92c2-4e72-a968-60cd5d8ebfe8"],
 " function and leave all your actual work to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["ParallelMap"]], "paclet:ref/ParallelMap"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->{"InlineFormula"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "7f022453-9aca-4b1d-8f05-d5624de9ad98"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1991,ExpressionUUID->"dc813632-65bb-4929-8649-a7d5f8470016"],

Cell["Raising and lowering: the Christoffel symbols", "Section",
 CellID->1992,ExpressionUUID->"daabb1a9-c04a-4822-9331-01d095ed6fe1"],

Cell["\<\
Next let us consider the more involved example of the Christoffel symbols. We \
decide to first compute the all-index-down components by feeding a \
(non-simplified) array that can be built up from what we have already \
computed:\
\>", "MathCaption",
 CellID->1993,ExpressionUUID->"56d7e31f-2aa9-4669-803c-fc193a654047"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"Christoffelcd", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"-", "\[ScriptM]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"-", "\[ScriptN]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"-", "\[ScriptP]"}]}], "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"%", " ", "//", " ", "ChristoffelToGradMetric"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ToArray", "[", "%", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[15]:=",
 CellID->1994,ExpressionUUID->"729492e8-da86-4af7-ac19-911b948cf495"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", 
        RowBox[{"-", 
         FractionBox[
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", 
            FractionBox[
             RowBox[{"4", " ", 
              InterpretationBox[
               StyleBox["r",
                ShowAutoStyles->False,
                AutoSpacing->False],
               $CellContext`r[],
               Editable->False], " ", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"\[LeftSkeleton]", "1", "\[RightSkeleton]"}], ")"}], 
              " ", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"2", " ", 
